{
 "about": "Field classes of the electrical domain's types for the house ledger (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.3, lint L-WATCH; WP-D electrical). 'fields' classifies every property name of house_sim/data/types/electrical.json and every field electrical's verbs, hooks and systems write onto its own types: ratings, kinds, wiring and printed text are identity; what the robot sets (switches, plugs and how they sit, cord routes and coils, settings, clocks and alarms, pairing, cable ends, slots, covers) is setting; what electrical derives from those every refresh (energized, live, powered, lit levels, displays, charging, link and boot states, alarm LEDs and states, readings) is process -- the setting that caused it is what the ledger compares -- except a lamp's lit, which the kernel's light allowance keeps a setting; damage and faults (scorched, tripped, burnt out, bent plugs, strained cords, kinks, leaks, ESD, corruption, cracked screens, water inside, a cord's walkway / rug / water / heat hazards) are condition with the worse direction; counters, test records and timestamps are bookkeeping. 'types' overrides a name where it means something else: a cell's condition word is wear (process; its leak is `leaking`), and the core light types electrical lights take its burnt_out / dim_level / flicker. water_sensitive: electrical gear whose electronics liquid reaches (physical.electrical_gear) and that no IP or weather rating protects -- so the kernel's ledger.water_sensitive is the one water-sensitivity predicate for electrical gear (phase-1 closeout_breakages row 6). Fields electrical writes onto other domains' entities are classified by the kernel's watch_fields.json (requests in catalog/analysis/phase2/handoff_WP-D_electrical.md).",
